    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "What is most interesting about DenseNet: the result itself, or the way it reframed the problem?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "DenseNet connected each layer to every later layer within a dense block. This encouraged feature reuse, improved gradient flow, and offered a compact alternative to simply making networks wider or deeper.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-densely-connected-convolutional-networks"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "That sounds like a promising direction. What mechanism actually makes it work?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Every layer receives the feature maps of all earlier layers in the same block.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-densely-connected-convolutional-networks"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "Why did the idea outlive one paper or experiment? What did later researchers actually inherit?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Experts generally treat DenseNet as an influential architecture for feature reuse and gradient flow, even when newer backbones are preferred in deployment. Its long-term legacy is the dense-connectivity pattern that clarified how short paths and reused features can improve deep CNNs.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-densely-connected-convolutional-networks"],
            "claimIds": ["claim-legacy-achievement-summary", "claim-legacy-description"],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "As today's systems grow larger, which lessons from DenseNet still matter, and which limits deserve to be questioned again?",
